Arrays through relays (benchmarks/gpu-pairs/gpupairs.m) on two GPUs, the
relays sending directly to those of the other GPU (MERK_GPU_PEER=1), on
1 MiB a measurement: every array comes back with its size and last element,
in all 5 chains. Built with -fopenmp, the relays have 8 worker teams each
(`workers 8`), which copy large arrays between the GPUs, and the program
takes OpenMP's devices: its sends still go directly (devices.h,
DeviceAllocateFine).
REQUIRES: two-gpus

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations -fdo-loops --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/gpu-pairs/gpupairs.m -o %t
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_GPU_PEER=1 timeout -k 1 300 %t 1 | awk '{ n++; if ($5 != $7) w++ } END { print n " rows, " w + 0 " wrong" }' | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines
CHECK: 90 rows, 0 wrong

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations -fdo-loops -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/gpu-pairs/gpupairs.m -o %t.omp
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_GPU_PEER=1 MERK_CHECK_DEVICE_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 300 %t.omp 1 workers 8 2> %t.err | awk '{ n++; if ($5 != $7) w++ } END { print n " rows, " w + 0 " wrong" }' | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DIRECT < %t.err
DIRECT: Mercury runtime: {{[1-9][0-9]*}} messages went directly between GPUs, and 0 of their copies were not given back
